  "readmeFile": "Readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.0:\n- BREAKING: callProveVerify, provePrefillIdentity and callProveTrustScore take a ConsentStatus, sent as Consent-Status, instead of always sending optedIn\n- BREAKING: Identity, Pre-Fill and TrustScore refuse a number with a leading or bracketed trunk 0, or a 00 prefix without a whole number after it, which was sent as a different number\n- BREAKING: callProveTrustScore gives ValueNone, not ValueSome 0, for a number refused here\n- FIXED: callProveVerify sent the state code as extendedAddress; it goes as region\n- FIXED: request bodies are UTF-8, so names outside ASCII reach Prove intact\n- FIXED: the sign-in form encodes its values\n- FIXED: a sign-in that fails or gives no token sends nothing further and returns the failure\n- FIXED: a non-200 answer without a readable error becomes an error naming the status\n- FIXED: dates of birth and added timestamps are Gregorian whatever the culture\n- FIXED: printing a license or an SMS or InstantLink request (%A, ToString) hides its keys and the person's number\n- FIXED: Readme examples match the API\n- FIXED: a UK number written +44 0 or 0044 0 drops the trunk 0; other country codes keep every digit\n- FIXED: a 2xx answer with an unreadable or empty body on any data call is that call's failure, with the status and the body's length and kind, not an exception or a success\n- FIXED: an answer of the typed InstantLink calls without a status is a failure, not a success with PhoneMatch = Yes\n- FIXED: callProveVerify fails on a response without a readable verified, instead of isDone = true and an exception in the caller\n- FIXED: failure text holds the status, the body's length and kind, and only named JSON error fields with digits and emails masked, never the body's text\n- FIXED: a refused number isn't echoed whole: the failure gives its digit count and at most its last two digits\n- BREAKING: Sms.send and InstantLink.generate refuse every number Identity refuses, such as 07700 900123",
